A handler updates a node carrying the program's own `#id` once per write.

NoReactivity writes each reader into the handler after the write, whatever the
node is called; html registered the node's updaters to run again at the end of
every handler touching what they read unless the node's id was one the
lowering named (`__nN`), so `#t`'s padding and text were written twice per
click (`inlineUpdated`).

deny out/none/html/index.html `addEventListener\("click", function\(\) \{(?:[^}]|\}[^)])*textContent(?:[^}]|\}[^)])*textContent` -- the text is written once per click
deny out/none/html/index.html `addEventListener\("click", function\(\) \{(?:[^}]|\}[^)])*setProperty(?:[^}]|\}[^)])*setProperty` -- and the padding
-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"

output {
    none {
        html
    }
}

component kept ui.node {
    var p ui.measurement = 16px
    var w = 1
    ui.vbox {
        ui.text #t(value="kept {w}", style={padding=p})
        ui.button #b(text="shrink", @click {
            p = 8px
            w = 2
        })
    }
}

ui.window {
    kept
}
